  "definition_ja": "ある数が別の数よりも大きいこと。a が b より大きいことを a > b と書き、等しい場合は含まない。",
  "definition_en": "Larger in value than another number; on a number line, the greater number is farther to the right. The symbol is >, as in 7 > 4.",
  "latex": "a > b",
  "spoken_en": "a is greater than b",
  "examples": [
    {
      "en": "Negative 2 is greater than negative 5 because it's farther to the right on the number line.",
      "ja": "−2 は −5 より大きい。数直線で右にあるからね。",
      "register": "spoken"
    },
    {
      "en": "List all integers that are greater than −3 and less than 2.",
      "ja": "−3 より大きく 2 より小さい整数を、すべて答えよ。",
      "register": "written"
    }
  ],
  "collocations": [],
  "pitfalls": [
    "「5 more than x」は x + 5 で、大小の比較ではなく足し算。「x は 5 より大きい」は x is greater than 5（x > 5）。",
    "「〜より大きい」「〜を超える」は境の数を含まない。境を含む「〜以上」は greater than or equal to（エントリ greater-than-or-equal-to）。",
    "不等号は左から読む。3 < x は 3 is less than x と読み、x > 3（x is greater than 3）と同じ意味。"
  ],
